<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 19:30:32 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Tsar Samuel laid to rest in Sofia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tsar-samuel-laid-to-rest-in-sofia</link><description>
In Bulgaria, the remains of medieval ruler Tsar Samuel have been laid to rest in the capital Sofia, after being flown back from the border with Greece by Bulgarian fighter jets. Their return follows decades of negotiations with Athens, in exchange for the return of religious artefacts. Nicholas Rushworth has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e04ee4e2-bfce-11f1-9ded-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-101231-101417-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e04ee4e2-bfce-11f1-9ded-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-101231-101417-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e512f18a-bfce-11f1-92d1-a1bfcac55e03</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 08:40:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Merz unveils new aid for Ukraine as Russia strikes Kyiv during German leader's visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-merz-unveils-new-aid-for-ukraine-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-during-german-leader-s-visit</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz announced a new aid package for Ukraine worth more than 1.3 billion euros ($1.5 billion) during a visit to Kyiv on Sunday marked by renewed Russian attacks on the Ukrainian capital, including the latest drone attack on a bridge spanning the Dnipro River.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/82db4916-c025-11f1-af15-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T115143Z-1568802837-RC29WNAM3HF4-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/82db4916-c025-11f1-af15-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T115143Z-1568802837-RC29WNAM3HF4-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">02137606-bfcf-11f1-bcb4-fb945a3fb0c8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 08:38:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/82db4916-c025-11f1-af15-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T115143Z-1568802837-RC29WNAM3HF4-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGE.jpg">© Reuters stringer</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany's Merz visits Kyiv as Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian cities</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/germany-s-merz-visits-kyiv-as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-cities</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz arrived in Ukraine's capital Kyiv on Sunday on an unannounced visit in a show of support for the country in its war with Russia. Merz's visit comes just a day after Russia warned foreigners and diplomats to leave the Ukrainian capital, saying that "massive" new airstrikes would hit the city. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv Gulliver Cragg has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92b6692c-bfc8-11f1-bdda-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-093117-093546-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92b6692c-bfc8-11f1-bdda-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-093117-093546-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">98181082-bfc8-11f1-87e1-57b3c23b77bb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 07:58:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: US wants to hold trilateral Ukraine talks with Russia by end of October, Zelensky says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-live-germany-s-merz-in-kyiv-for-talks-with-zelensky</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Sunday that the US wants to broker a new round of talks with Ukraine and Russia on ending the war and hold it by the end of October. Earlier, Kyiv Mayor Vitali Klitschko said the city's Northern Bridge over the Dnipro River was again hit in a Russian attack during a visit by German Chancellor Friedrich Merz. Follow our liveblog for all the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0324a9be-bfe5-11f1-abdb-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277313191571.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0324a9be-bfe5-11f1-abdb-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277313191571.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f62f0f32-bfc2-11f1-94c5-21597aa5b1df</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 07:28:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0324a9be-bfe5-11f1-abdb-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277313191571.jpg">© Evgeniy Maloletka, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bosnia votes in general election with wartime divisions still dominating</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bosnia-votes-in-general-election-with-wartime-divisions-still-dominating</link><description>
Bosnia is heading to the polls on Sunday after a general election campaign dominated by parties that identify closely with the ethnic divisions of its 1990s war. Voters will elect a vast number of officials across multiple tiers of government, in a complex system that has held the partitioned country together since the 1995 peace deal. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Belgrade Laurent Rouy has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2691dfe8-bfbd-11f1-9fa4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-081237-081823-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2691dfe8-bfbd-11f1-9fa4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-081237-081823-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2bb8a006-bfbd-11f1-b334-810f6be85510</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 06:51:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Bosnians vote as pro-Russian politician looms large and ethnic tensions simmer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261004-polls-open-in-bosnia-and-herzegovina-as-pro-russian-politician-looms-large-over-race</link><description>
Bosnians head to the polls Sunday in elections that ​could impact how much influence Russia has over the small Balkan nation, with separatist Serb leader Milorad Dodik dominating the campaign despite his ban from public office. Bosnia and Herzegovina, a country marred by ethnic tensions, has struggled to recover since its brutal 1992-95 conflict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ecf760d8-bfb6-11f1-a5f3-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277206578071.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ecf760d8-bfb6-11f1-a5f3-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277206578071.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f34530f6-bfb5-11f1-be74-f9987177d2cc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 05:55:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ecf760d8-bfb6-11f1-a5f3-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277206578071.jpg">© Armin Durgut, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Latvia's PM on track to lead pro-Ukraine coalition after parliamentary election victory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-latvia-elections-pm-kulbergs-pro-ukraine-party-ahead-coalition-partners-stumble</link><description>
Latvian ​Prime Minister Andris Kulbergs was set to retain power and form a coalition after his centrist United List won parliamentary elections on Sunday, the biggest in the country's post-independence history. While the result is expected to reinforce the Baltic country’s pro-European and pro-Ukrainian stance, populist parties also made significant gains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2928feea-bf6c-11f1-8285-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-03T092541Z-1228379656-RC2KVNAISL7K-RTRMADP-3-LATVIA-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2928feea-bf6c-11f1-8285-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-03T092541Z-1228379656-RC2KVNAISL7K-RTRMADP-3-LATVIA-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fe836c84-bf6b-11f1-8fbb-adf8d4402a4f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 20:58:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2928feea-bf6c-11f1-8285-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-03T092541Z-1228379656-RC2KVNAISL7K-RTRMADP-3-LATVIA-ELECTION.jpg">© Ints Kalnins, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Putin's war for the history books: Dmytro Kuleba speaks to France 24</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261003-putin-s-war-for-the-history-books-dmytro-kuleba-speaks-to-france-24</link><description>
The Bronze Horseman, the iconic equestrian statue in Senate Square in St Petersburg, was commissioned by Catherine the Great in honor of Peter the Great, the city's founder. The pedestal of the statue bears a laconic dedication, "To Peter the First, Catherine the Second, 1782". Does Putin want to be the third, Vladimir the Great? And is that ambition, expansion at any cost, the real reason behind the war in Ukraine? According to Former Ukrainian Foreign Minister Dmytro Kuleba, "Putin only cares about what will be written about him in history books."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39db6df8-bf4f-11f1-a837-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20813474576ac13a318fedb5-47858484.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39db6df8-bf4f-11f1-a837-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20813474576ac13a318fedb5-47858484.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">786fb938-bf55-11f1-89fa-77fcee9429f1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 18:08:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Italy’s Ustica enigma: Can French files solve mystery crash blamed on stray missile?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-italy-ustica-enigma-can-french-files-solve-mystery-crash-blamed-on-stray-missile-gaddafi</link><description>
France’s decision to share defence documents with the Italian judiciary has raised hopes of a breakthrough in investigations into the 1980 crash of a passenger jet near the island of Ustica, which a former Italian president claimed was mistakenly shot down by a French fighter jet. Sceptics caution that the files are unlikely to shed light on one of Italy’s most enduring mysteries, let alone reveal a culprit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc7cbc12-bf35-11f1-9acd-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23245467521507.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc7cbc12-bf35-11f1-9acd-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23245467521507.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef2ca75e-bf35-11f1-a25e-f7121f11def5</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 15:42:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cc7cbc12-bf35-11f1-9acd-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23245467521507.jpg">© Emiliano Grillotti, AP</source><dc:creator>Benjamin DODMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Fresh protests over housing flare in Spain after lawmakers reject relief measures</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-fresh-protests-over-housing-flare-spain-after-lawmakers-reject-relief-measures</link><description>
Tens of thousands of protesters marched in Madrid and other cities in Spain on Saturday to demand affordable housing, fuelled by anger at lawmakers who narrowly rejected measures put forward by the government of Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez to strengthen protection for tenants.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9be2eeca-bf29-11f1-9e39-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T144436Z-1967364448-RC22VNA86KAV-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING-PARLIAMENT-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9be2eeca-bf29-11f1-9e39-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T144436Z-1967364448-RC22VNA86KAV-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING-PARLIAMENT-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb6e52fe-bf2b-11f1-8432-8dd51af6e59d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:20:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9be2eeca-bf29-11f1-9e39-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T144436Z-1967364448-RC22VNA86KAV-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-HOUSING-PARLIAMENT-PROTEST.jpg">©  Alejandro Martinez Velez, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia strikes another Kyiv bridge, deepening travel chaos in Ukraine's capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261003-russia-strikes-another-major-bridge-in-kyiv</link><description>
Kyiv's Northern Bridge across the Dnipro river was hit by a Russian air attack, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said Saturday, deepening travel chaos amid an escalation in strikes ​on ‌infrastructure in the Ukrainian capital. The latest attack comes a day after the city's Southern Bridge was hit by several strikes that officials said were "tearing Kyiv apart".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea2cd384-bef2-11f1-b2ef-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T171441Z-992305596-RC22VNAD0WX5-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea2cd384-bef2-11f1-b2ef-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T171441Z-992305596-RC22VNAD0WX5-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49ec0670-bee7-11f1-9ba8-cfe4814e5241</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 06:40:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea2cd384-bef2-11f1-b2ef-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-02T171441Z-992305596-RC22VNAD0WX5-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV-BRIDGE.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>'We have to close defence gaps urgently': EU Parliament Foreign Affairs Committee chief McAllister</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-we-have-to-close-defence-gaps-urgently-eu-parliament-foreign-affairs-committee-chief-mcallister</link><description>
We sit down with David McAllister, the chair of the European Parliament’s Foreign Affairs Committee. He talks to us about the security threats facing Europe, and what defence gaps the EU urgently needs to close. For McAllister, the EU is "not at war with the Russian Federation, but we are no longer at peace with Russia". He also believes that the EU is not, as yet, capable of making sovereign decisions in certain areas of defence "because we are too dependent on US capabilities."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dffc4efa-bdab-11f1-8164-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-MCALLISTER.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dffc4efa-bdab-11f1-8164-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-MCALLISTER.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a554d442-bbfe-11f1-89dc-9759d9709271</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 15:57:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Spanish lawmakers vote down affordable housing bills in blow to Sanchez’s government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-spanish-lawmakers-vote-down-affordable-housing-bills-in-blow-to-sanchez-s-government</link><description>
Demonstrators protesting against Spain's housing crisis reacted with fury on Friday after the country's parliament rejected two bills put forward by the government that centre-left Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez hoped would address their concerns. Rents have doubled over the past decade, with average prices now almost equivalent to the average young person's monthly salary.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b933cd3e-be73-11f1-ab4c-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/25a8cb04b47e7911259db45cdda5dc36ccb9daf2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b933cd3e-be73-11f1-ab4c-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/25a8cb04b47e7911259db45cdda5dc36ccb9daf2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba3d9962-be73-11f1-bb42-f1d54a98d11b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 15:12:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b933cd3e-be73-11f1-ab4c-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/25a8cb04b47e7911259db45cdda5dc36ccb9daf2.jpg">© Thomas Coex, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>A grim winter ahead? EU states asked to prepare gas and electricity savings</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261002-a-grim-winter-ahead-eu-states-asked-to-prepare-gas-and-electricity-savings</link><description>
Alarm bells are ringing about fuel prices across the EU. The average cost of diesel per litre is well above €2, whereas in October of last year it was around €1.50. Even before this latest spike, the cost of living was already biting, and it seems that the conflict in the Middle East is not going to give Europeans much respite as the winter draws closer. We review what EU member states have done to cushion the blow of rising energy prices for ordinary people, and whether those measures have been effective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44ba510-bcea-11f1-b5f9-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-TALKING-EUROPE-DEBAT.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44ba510-bcea-11f1-b5f9-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-TALKING-EUROPE-DEBAT.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">90629a96-bbff-11f1-8896-bf034f3d69d4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 15:10:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>G7 members will release 100 million barrels of diesel after US threatens export ban</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-eu-fully-rejects-us-threat-to-ban-diesel-exports-unless-bloc-releases-more-fuel-stocks</link><description>
Members of the Group of Seven bloc of highly industrialised economies on Friday agreed to release 100 million barrels of diesel and crude oil from their reserves over four months, averting a potential US ban on diesel exports. The European Union had earlier pushed back against Washington's threat, with an EU official saying the 27-member bloc “fully” rejected the move.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79380082-be51-11f1-8df4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268371284984.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79380082-be51-11f1-8df4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268371284984.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3b095bac-be52-11f1-b210-f7e877f55dc1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 11:15:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79380082-be51-11f1-8df4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26268371284984.jpg">© Michael Probst, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA[As Europe's balance of power shifts eastward, France & Spain seek to 'reinforce their own positions']]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-as-europe-s-balance-of-power-shifts-eastward-france-spain-seek-to-reinforce-their-own-positions-1</link><description>
Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Carlos Mascarell Vilar, political scientist based in Spain. From his own perspective, Emmanuel Macron's visit to Spain needs to be understood by European power, political legacy, and geoeconomics. France and Spain are seeking to reinforce their bilateral relationship at a moment when the balance of power within Europe is changing rapidly, particularly with the growing importance of countries in the east such as Poland. For Macron, strengthening the Madrid-Paris axis is also part of a broader effort to advance European defence and strategic sovereignty.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97253450-be44-11f1-823b-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-131041-131704-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97253450-be44-11f1-823b-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-131041-131704-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9cad007e-be44-11f1-bf8d-dd722e4b5c5c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 09:49:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia is ‘tearing Kyiv apart’, mayor says, as Moscow’s bombing brings traffic to a halt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-live-russia-hits-kyiv-s-southern-bridge-as-moscow-continues-to-pound-capital</link><description>
Russia is “tearing Kyiv apart”, the city’s Mayor Vitali Klitschko said on Friday, as Russia pummelled key infrastructure across the Ukrainian capital. Russian drones have pummelled Kyiv’s Southern Bridge, forcing authorities to close traffic on it. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
